    "review_findings": [
      "Use the same public acknowledgement for eligible, unknown and held requests in each supported locale. The conditional message makes no claim of email delivery.",
      "Opening the confirmation page does not confirm Recovery or change credentials. GET does not consume proof. Explicit Continue can consume proof and can place a governed hold when stronger assurance is required.",
      "The credential form may appear after proof acceptance even for a held case. The wording ties credential replacement and revocation of active sessions and trusted-device assurance to successful completion. Further assurance can prevent completion.",
      "The unavailable state covers multiple outcomes. The existing request route offers a way back. The wording makes support conditional because the current router provides no Help or Contact Support route.",
      "The completion text directs a fresh sign-in after committed completion or the same committed operation receipt. The controller clears the browser session. The current template targets /login, and the router has no GET /login. WELL-183 AC4 must exercise the allowed destination and successful sign-in through the actual browser journey."
    ],
